      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1933570340531106124",
      "text": "[5:58PM] #Alausa_Ikeja #TrafficUpdate \n\n On Obafemi Awolowo Way, movement from Barrack, Coca-Cola junction, Radio, and Allen junction towards Balogun is generally good. However, traffic becomes busy approaching Olowu junction leading to the Ikeja underneath bridge due to spillover from the Ikeja Along overpass. The return journey on this axis is moving as expected but experiences congestion near Allen junction and Radio junction, respectively. \n\nProceeding towards Alausa, the traffic flow is good until the vicinity of Dr. Nurudeen Olowopopo by the traffic light, where it becomes busy.\nLateef Jakande Road is experiencing a faster pace of movement from Coca-Cola junction, LTV8, Mobil, and Cadbury towards the first gate. However, the stretch from Wemco junction to Omole roundabout shows steady movement, with the return journey reported to be proceeding well.\n\nOther corridors within the zone, including Mobolaji Johnson Avenue in both inward and outward directions, Adeniyi Jones inward and outward, and the stretch of Dr. Nurudeen Olowopopo connecting to Otedola underneath the bridge, are all reported to be in good condition. No traffic impediments have been sighted, and officers are actively managing traffic flow as needed.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
